MEDICAL DISCLAIMER:

This tool is intended for use by qualified healthcare professionals only as 
a clinical decision support aid. It does not:

  • Replace clinical judgment or comprehensive patient assessment
  • Generate diagnoses
  • Provide treatment recommendations beyond referral screening
  • Account for patient-specific contraindications or preferences

The treating physician remains solely responsible for all clinical decisions.

SCOPE OF APPLICATION:

This tool is developed and validated for use in secondary care settings for 
patients diagnosed with idiopathic Parkinson disease who have not previously 
been treated with a device-aided therapy (DAT) and in whom oral and 
transdermal treatment is conducted according to current guidelines (including 
dose fractionation and, where indicated, use of dopamine agonists, MAO-B 
inhibitors, COMT inhibitors and/or amantadine).

IMPORTANT LIMITATION:

This tool is likely insufficiently sensitive for patients with therapy-
resistant tremor for whom deep brain stimulation (DBS) may be considered 
regardless of the score.

